## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Secrets. Every rule below exists because the file it names has, in some
## project somewhere, been committed by accident -- and a credential in git
## history stays there after the commit is amended away. Do not relax them.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
set-env.ps1
set-env.sh
*.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.azure/
entra-app-config-*.json
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json
secrets.json

## OAuth runtime state. Encrypted at rest, but this is delegated access to real drives --
## it is per-deployment state, not source, and has no business in a repository.
oauth-state.json
entra-refresh-tokens.json
dp-keys/

## Local run artefacts. *.log is deliberately broad: the explicit names kept
## missing new ones (last-gateway-test-run.log was unmatched for weeks).
*.log
.mcp-session.json
preview-*.html
.tmp-secret-backup.txt

